Sources for `refactoring` skill (see plans/skill-audits/refactoring.md for full audit):

- Kent Beck "Tidy First?" 2023 — https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/tidy-first/9781098151232/ — separate Tidyings from Behavior Changes, Two-Hat principle
- Martin Fowler "Refactoring" 2nd ed. 2018 — https://martinfowler.com/books/refactoring.html — catalog of named refactors + smells catalog
- Michael Feathers "Working Effectively with Legacy Code" 2004 — Sprout Method, Wrap Method for legacy/untested code
- citypaul/.dotfiles refactor notes — Tidy-First commit cadence
- Joshua Kerievsky "Refactoring to Patterns" — referenced, used sparingly (not daily practice)

Strategy: distill. Author for void-harness with two modes mirroring tdd. Reject monolithic-rewrite framing. Companion hooks: tidying-commit-prefix, refactor-named-grep. Allowed Fowler names in ../../hooks/fowler-refactors.txt.
